{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016fh8dLEZdZj2eqWanTga3y","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 48646a049ada84a62ca0df299f3254c52731ca4d\nAuthor: diytechy <78943505+diytechy@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Sep 3 00:53:08 2026 -0500\n\n    WI-579: close at the round-015 rework, and retract an ambiguous red\n    \n    The close ritual at the rework tip. The spec already sits in\n    docs/archive/work/complete/ with an empty `specref`; this fills the Deliverable\n    with the round-015 account, refreshes docs/ratify/CURRENT.md at the spine\n    amendments this round made (LLR-207, LLR-208, IF-175, TC-205, TC-206 — all\n    still `Drafted`; no Status flipped, no last_approved written), and lands the\n    figures.\n    \n    FULL UNFILTERED SUITE at `2b4be13c`: 3345 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in\n    612.94s. Smoke at the closing tip: 1506 passed, 8 skipped in 32.72s; budget\n    47.6s vs 60s -> within.\n    \n    AND A RETRACTION, because the earlier rounds' phrasing was doing work it had\n    not earned. The one failure is\n    `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`, which\n    rounds 007 and 012 recorded as \"bisected clean at the integration base\" — a\n    sentence that reads as INHERITED. It is not. I drove the base in a scratch\n    worktree and `0ecc62b` PASSES the test, so this red is CAUSED by this branch:\n    its spine amendments moved the derived stage fingerprint.\n    \n    Benign, and now for a stated reason rather than a hopeful one. `docs/stage` is\n    declared `[generated]` and belongs to the trunk lane; `git diff 0ecc62b..HEAD\n    -- docs/stage` is empty because a work branch must not commit it; `check.py`'s\n    own `derived-stage` step reports `SKIP work branch ... generated freshness is\n    the trunk lane's` here by design; and `trunk_step.py --regen` regenerates it\n    after the merge (concurrency-restructure §5.2). Caused-but-benign and inherited\n    are different claims and only one of them is true, so the Deliverable and the\n    fragment now say which.\n    \n    Deferred open items: none.\n    \n    WI: WI-579\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n=== trailer:\nrounds 007 and 012 recorded as \"bisected clean at the integration base\" — a\nsentence that reads as INHERITED. It is not. I drove the base in a scratch\nworktree and `0ecc62b` PASSES the test, so this red is CAUSED by this branch:\nits spine amendments moved the derived stage fingerprint.\n\nBenign, and now for a stated reason rather than a hopeful one. `docs/stage` is\ndeclared `[generated]` and belongs to the trunk lane; `git diff 0ecc62b..HEAD\n-- docs/stage` is empty because a work branch must not commit it; `check.py`'s\nown `derived-stage` step reports `SKIP work branch ... generated freshness is\nthe trunk lane's` here by design; and `trunk_step.py --regen` regenerates it\nafter the merge (concurrency-restructure §5.2). Caused-but-benign and inherited\nare different claims and only one of them is true, so the Deliverable and the\nfragment now say which.\n\nDeferred open items: none.\n\nWI: WI-579\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e54a6b5-0cf0-4e13-8bd2-bc5fdc31d7d4","uuid":"b3cedb18-3156-4c0b-bdb6-c01f5365accc","timestamp":"2026-09-03T05:54:33.453Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 48646a049ada84a62ca0df299f3254c52731ca4d\nAuthor: diytechy <78943505+diytechy@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Sep 3 00:53:08 2026 -0500\n\n    WI-579: close at the round-015 rework, and retract an ambiguous red\n    \n    The close ritual at the rework tip. The spec already sits in\n    docs/archive/work/complete/ with an empty `specref`; this fills the Deliverable\n    with the round-015 account, refreshes docs/ratify/CURRENT.md at the spine\n    amendments this round made (LLR-207, LLR-208, IF-175, TC-205, TC-206 — all\n    still `Drafted`; no Status flipped, no las