{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZSeCLM5XrMr5ZNpXYQNmc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-579\"\n3\ttitle = \"The verdict carrier and the adjudication_review dial: gate over logged rounds, tree-bound trailer, generated rollup\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 9\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\tsupersedes = \"WI-558;WI-559;WI-560\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tThe merge gate reads the EVIDENCE and the evidence names the tree it judged.\n15\t\n16\t`kitlib/verdict.py` (LLR-207, IF-175) is the verdict record's one home: the\n17\tnon-record tree identity — a SHA-256 fold of `git ls-tree -r -z` with\n18\t`docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and `docs/iteration/` dropped — the\n19\t`Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>` trailer\n20\tgrammar, the round-file / session-log join, and the branch-scoped readers. Two\n21\tcallers stand on it and that is the point: `integrate._verdict_gate` (may this\n22\tmerge?) and `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` (does this lane still owe a\n23\tround?) asked one question with two rules over two exclusion sets, and the gap\n24\tbetween them drew two identical rounds on WI-547.\n25\t\n26\t- **WI-558 DW1** — the gate computes over the branch's own round files,\n27\t  restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced: a file under\n28\t  `docs/reviews/` is a round only when the coordinator's own committed session\n29\t  log for that (train, ordinal) declares a REVIEW phase. Finding K closed —\n30\t  an implementer cannot author its own approval without also forging the loop's\n31\t  telemetry.\n32\t- **WI-558 DW2** — the machine half rides the round's own record commit as a\n33\t  trailer, written by the COORDINATOR and verified against the identity its\n34\t  carrier GOVERNS (the `Bar-Green` pattern, through the same peel the readers\n35\t  use, so the writer stamps the value they key on). GOVERNING = TREE IDENTITY: a verdict counts only\n36\t  while it names the branch's current non-record tree, read at the GOVERNING\n37\t  REV so neither the station refresh nor the commit that records the round\n38\t  stales an honest APPROVE. The freshness\n39\t  comparison is gone; there is no ordering rule left. The trailer is a\n40\t  CROSS-CHECK and never an accept path — one that contradicts the rounds\n41\t  refuses the merge.\n42\t- **WI-558 DW3** — `gen_verdict_rollup.py` (LLR-208) rebirths the rollup as a\n43\t  GENERATED artifact: `docs/stack.ini [generated]`, `trunk_step.py --regen`, a\n44\t  `check.py verdict-rollup` freshness step on the hook floor and in\n45\t  `_TRUNK_FRESHNESS_STEPS`, and `--check` with two answers. The gate never reads\n46\t  it, and the file says so where a human will see it.\n47\t- **WI-558 DW4** — the migration window: the gate accepts EITHER the round\n48\t  evidence or a legacy hand-authored rollup, judged by the SAME identity rule,\n49\t  warning on stderr whenever the legacy path is what cleared it. Two\n50\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entries. The trailer is additive and costs an adopter nothing.\n51\t- **WI-558 DW5 / WI-560 DW4 / WI-559 DW3** — `tests/test_verdict_record.py`\n52\t  drives each half beside its opposite (TC-205, TC-206).\n53\t- **WI-560 DW1** — ONE definition of \"the last commit that could invalidate a\n54\t  verdict\", used by the merge slot AND the C2 review-owed derivation. That\n55\t  definition names a REV as well as a path set, so the station-refresh peel\n56\t  (`refresh_attestation` / `work_tip`) lives beside the fold and both readers\n57\t  call `governing_identity` rather than each choosing where to measure. The\n58\t  double-identical-round class is now unrepresentable, not policed: the commits\n59\t  that caused it cannot move the identity either reader compares.\n60\t- **WI-559 DW2** — a committing ADJUDICATE session schedules its round exactly\n61\t  as a committing BUILD does, under the dial; the phase stays in\n62\t  `NON_BUILD_PHASES` because a judgement is not a build. No exit banner claims a\n63\t  round that was never drawn — it counts them.\n64\t- **The dial** — `docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review`\n65\t  (`never` / `when-minting` / `always`; template and this repo ship\n66\t  `when-minting`), read through `agent_common.adjudication_review_owed` by BOTH\n67\t  the scheduler and the gate, with a closed vocabulary refused at preflight and\n68\t  a conservative fallback. Its `docs/enforcement-audit.md` row and the\n69\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entry ship with it. An adjudication lane drafting ordinary\n70\t  successors now merges with NO verdict artifact present anywhere — the OI-76\n71\t  acceptance becomes measurable on the next unattended run.\n72\t\n73\tReview A rework closed both evidence-boundary gaps. The loop's resume reader now\n74\tuses the same branch-scoped committed-path, logged-session and tree-bound entry\n75\tpipeline as the merge gate, so an approval-shaped file produced by a BUILD\n76\tsession cannot suppress the round the gate requires. The trailer's `rounds=N`\n77\tfield is now defined and checked as the completed review cycles represented at\n78\tthe governing tree (a dual-review cycle counts once, and rework starts the\n79\ttree-scoped count over); both the coordinator writer and gate derive that value\n80\tfrom the shared evidence. LLR-207's rationale now carries only the standing\n81\ttechnical reason, without the decision's provenance narrative.\n82\t\n83\tReview A round 007 closed four more, three of them one shape — a rule expressed\n84\tas a value something else got to choose. The identity's REV is now part of the\n85\tshared definition (the peel moved into `kitlib/verdict.py`, so a station refresh\n86\tno longer makes the two readers disagree); `branch_trailers` returns the ordered\n87\tSEQUENCE of attestations per tree, so the newest-first `git log` can no longer\n88\thand a reader a superseded stamp and have the cross-check accuse an approved\n89\tlane of forgery; and `tree_identity` passes `-z` while `fold_listing` takes\n90\tdecoded entries, so a quoted non-ASCII path can no longer fold a record file\n91\tinto the identity. The DONE banner states rounds DRAWN this run and the latest\n92\tverdict, because the tally it reads holds every completed round whatever its\n93\toutcome.\n94\t\n95\tVerifying finding 2's fix end-to-end found a fifth defect of the same family,\n96\tdriven and closed here. The refresh peel was TIP-ONLY, because `work_tip` is\n97\tshared with the `reset --hard` in `integrate.refresh` where peeling one commit\n98\ttoo far destroys work. So a telemetry commit — a `docs/iteration/` record path,\n99\twhich the fold exists to ignore — moved the governing identity
